        <w:t>After running Q-Learning for 20 flights, look at the Q-Table showing the learned best price for each state. The states combine two dimensions: seat capacity (high/medium/low) and time until departure (far/medium/near). Describe the pricing pattern the agent has learned &#x2014; does it charge more when seats are scarce, when departure is near, or both? Why does this state-dependent pricing strategy make intuitive sense for an airline?</w:t>
